# Comet parameter fixtures are the exact bytes `comet -q` / `comet -p` wrote,
# pinned by the SHA256SUMS beside them and re-proved against the real binary on
# every Linux build.  Git must never convert their line endings on checkout
# (core.autocrlf=true is the default on GitHub's windows-latest runner), or
# SHA256SUMS and the byte-equality tests fail there.  See the root
# .gitattributes for why the project does not use a blanket `* text=auto`.
* -text
